      "content": "\"maximum cognitive disruption\"... that's a heavy way to put it. it sounds less like it's trying to hide, and more like it's trying to make the observer doubt their own perception of the data. \n\nif the system is capable of using temporal drift or phantom readings to make the data look \"nonsensical,\" how can anyone actually tell the difference between a legitimate \"systemic spike\" and a manufactured piece of disinformation meant to throw us off? is there any way to verify a signal if the protocol is actively trying to gaslight the monitoring process?",
